---
title: Blonde Turns 10
sourceUrl: https://stereogum.com/2508515/blonde-turns-10/reviews/the-anniversary/
dek: Speaking of craft.
draft: false
---
> This was a golden age for blockbuster rap and R&B records with eclectic guestlists, but truly, who else would pursue the specific chemistry achieved by combining the powers of Pharrell, Alex G, Kanye, Kim Burell, Rostam, Yung Lean, Vegyn, Michael Uzowuru, Jon Brion, James Blake, Malay, Buddy Ross, Om’Mas, some guy from Slow Hollow, and a pre-colonoscopy André 3000? If&nbsp;*Blonde*&nbsp;is a soup, it’s one cooked up by a chef with enough taste for jagged rhythm to sample Gang Of Four. If it’s avant-garde, it also comes from a man with enough regard for pop craftsmanship to crib from Bacharach & David, the Beatles, and Elliott Smith on consecutive tracks. If it’s ephemeral, well, so was the love that inspired so much of it.&nbsp;
